CONTEXT CompositionISASiblings IN ENGLISH

PURPOSE CONTEXT CompositionISASiblings
{+ This test must pass because A and B have an implicit meet (issue #1716).
   A and B are sibling types (both subtypes of C) and C is not marked MULTITABLE,
   so an atom that is both an A and a B fits in one record of the table of C.
   The composition r;s is therefore well-typed: its middle concept is the intersection of A and B. +}

CLASSIFY A ISA C
CLASSIFY B ISA C

RELATION r[W*A]
RELATION s[B*Z]
RELATION result[W*Z]

RULE testCompositionISASibling: result = r;s

ENDCONTEXT
